<%# The tooltips travel as VALUES on the controller element: Stimulus reads them off
    this.element, and set on the child button they were invisible — the text fell through to
    the English fallback. %>
<div data-controller="filter-persistence"
     data-filter-persistence-storage-id-value="<%= storage_id %>"
     data-filter-persistence-enabled-value="<%= enabled? %>"
     data-filter-persistence-enabled-tooltip-value="<%= enabled_tooltip %>"
     data-filter-persistence-disabled-tooltip-value="<%= disabled_tooltip %>">
  <%# `Bali::Tooltip` and not daisyUI's `tooltip` class: daisyUI lays its hidden balloon out
      as a `::before` of the button, and with the button at the toolbar's edge that box
      overflowed the scroll container — measured on `data_table/with_filter_persistence` at
      812px, the page scrolled to 901 with nothing visible past 812 (#1392). This balloon only
      exists while it is open, portaled to the body. The `tooltip` target is how
      filter-persistence-controller.js keeps its text in step with the state (updateTooltip). %>
  <%= render Bali::Tooltip::Component.new(placement: :bottom,
                                          data: { filter_persistence_target: "tooltip" }) do |balloon| %>
    <% balloon.with_trigger do %>
      <%# Explicit aria-label: both icons are `aria-hidden` svgs and the label is only uncovered
          inside the ⋯, so without this the button has no accessible name. It matches the
          visible text so "Label in Name" does not break wherever that label does show.

          `aria-pressed` is the ONLY thing exposing which state it is in: the icon swap is
          visual, and the balloon describes the wrapper tippy is anchored to, not the button.
          Without it the button announces the same on as off, and since the click reloads
          through Turbo announcing nothing, there was no way to tell which way it landed. The
          JS keeps it current (updateUI). %>
      <button type="button"
              class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm gap-2"
              data-action="filter-persistence#toggle"
              data-filter-persistence-target="button"
              aria-pressed="<%= enabled? %>"
              aria-label="<%= label %>">
        <span data-filter-persistence-target="iconEnabled" class="<%= 'hidden' unless enabled? %>">
          <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new('bookmark-check', class: 'w-5 h-5 text-primary') %>
        </span>
        <span data-filter-persistence-target="iconDisabled" class="<%= 'hidden' if enabled? %>">
          <%= render Bali::Icon::Component.new('bookmark', class: 'w-5 h-5 text-base-content/55') %>
        </span>
        <%# No `sm:inline`, on purpose: in the toolbar this is an icon control. Inside the ⋯
            the control takes a whole row and a bare icon is anonymous there, so the unlayered
            rule in data_table/index.css uncovers it there and only there. `btn-square` is left
            off the button's class for the same reason: it would force width = height and the
            label would overflow. %>
        <span class="toolbar-control-label hidden"><%= label %></span>
      </button>
    <% end %>
    <%= tooltip %>
  <% end %>
</div>
